      "title": "Crude faces volatile week as W Asia supply risks keep mkts tense: Analysts",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/crude-faces-volatile-week-as-w-asia-supply-risks-keep-mkts-tense-analysts-126101800427_1.html",
      "description": "Crude oil prices are poised for another volatile week, with supply worries in West Asia keeping markets on edge and stalled US-Iran talks adding to fears of fresh disruptions, even as efforts to ease shortages offer some relief, analysts said.\nInvestors will track weekly crude stocks data from the American Petroleum Institute (API), Cushing inventories, overall US oil stocks and crude imports for signals on the supply-demand balance.\nThe Strait of Hormuz remains a key source of uncertainty, with any disruption to shipments through the critical waterway threatening to further tighten global supplies.\nThe domestic commodities market will remain closed during the morning session on Tuesday due to Dussehra.\n\"Our outlook remains cautiously bullish, with price movements likely to be driven primarily by geopolitical developments and actual supply disruptions rather than headlines alone,\" said Ajit Mishra, SVP of Research at Religare Broking.\nRecent declines in US crude inventories have .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-18T13:25:50"
    },
    {
      "title": "Earnings, crude oil, Jio IPO key monitorables for investors next week",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/earnings-crude-oil-jio-ipo-key-monitorables-for-investors-next-week-126101800241_1.html",
      "description": "Quarterly earnings, crude oil, Jio Platforms' initial public offering and trading activity of foreign investors will drive investors' sentiment in a holiday-shortened week ahead, analysts said.\nBesides, developments in West Asia and the rupee-dollar trend would be tracked by investors.\n\"Indian equities enter the coming week with improved momentum following two consecutive weekly advances and a strong recovery led by information technology stocks. The sustainability of this move remains to be established. Elevated crude oil prices, geopolitical uncertainty, global bond market movements and uneven market breadth continue to warrant caution.\n\"Investors are likely to focus on whether the recent rally broadens beyond IT stocks and whether the benchmark indices can sustain their gains above immediate resistance levels,\" Ponmudi R, CEO - Enrich Money, an online trading and wealth tech firm, said.\nThe proposed Jio Platforms IPO, which will open on October 21, is another key event to watch,",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-18T07:25:37"
    }
